      "math_academy_id": "q-66712",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "The equation ${log}_{64}⁡4=\\frac{1}{3}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt[3]{b}=4.$ What is the value of $b?$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{64}⁡4=\\frac{1}{3}$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=4,$ $b=64,$ and $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation is equivalent to ${64}^{1/3}=4,$ which is also equivalent to $\\sqrt[3]{64}=4.$ Consequently, $b=64.$",
